reading (honest):
- resources match the published spec (4 vCPU / ~15.6 GiB) but every job is ONE machine: SUT, generator and storage would be co-located. classify() => reduced_R177_only on all 6; closes R-177_full/R-178/R-179 = false.
- x64 reproducibility is poor: three different CPU models in three jobs (EPYC 7763 / 9V74 / 9V45), so the same test lands on different hardware run to run; one job had CPU CV 0.137 (noisy) vs 0.008-0.010 in the others.
- x64 effective parallel cores 1.50-1.88 of 4 (scaling efficiency ~0.38-0.47). Probable cause: the 4 vCPU are SMT siblings (~2 physical cores) - NOT verified (no lscpu topology captured); short 0.17 s window also includes process start overhead. Either way 4 vCPU here is not 4 cores of throughput.
- arm64 is steady (CV <=0.003, 2.86-3.19 effective cores) but the project's requirements.lock does not install on arm64 (log 381) - a supply-chain change is needed first.
- jobs cannot accept connections from each other => no 3-node separation; 6 h per job => no 24 h soak. The owner's directive excludes treating Actions as an isolated-environment substitute; consistent with these measurements.
- verdict: GitHub-hosted runners are NOT eligible for approved R-177..R-181 measurement. Usable only for L0 reproducibility/health checks.
